  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 589a77387c7c4ea488d9368fe6c3cd2f, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dialogue 2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Axion
  dialogues:
  - Here you can see the complete production line of the TRANSFORMER.
  - In general, a TRANSFORMER takes a sequence of resources (also known as TOKENS),
    which it then represents in an abstract way called an EMBEDDING. The EMBEDDING
    tries to contain as much of the semantic, syntactic, and contextual meaning of
    the TOKENS as possible.
  - This EMBEDDING is created via a clever mechanism called ATTENTION, which tries
    to learn the relationships and context of each TOKEN within the given SEQUENCE.
    These relationships can then be compared to the learned relationships of the
    possible output TOKENS.
  - Finally, this comparison is used to determine which possible output TOKEN is
    expected to be produced. Though this is a probabilistic output, with enough training
    the TRANSFORMER can guess the correct output TOKEN.
  - Pfew...
  - Don't worry! I know it can seem like a lot, but we'll guide you through each
    part step-by-step.
